/* book exam traps: Dropping the factor 2 in λB = 2 neff Λ. Without it the pitch comes out double (1069 nm instead of 534.5 nm for 1550 nm). | Treating excess loss and insertion loss as the same number. Excess loss compares the total output with the input; insertion loss compares one port with the input. | Measuring the coupling ratio against the input power instead of the total output. CR is a share of what comes out: 118/230, not 118/250. | Swapping isolation and insertion loss on an isolator. Isolation is the large reverse attenuation (30 to 60 dB); insertion loss is the small forward penalty (0.5 to 1 dB). | Drawing an add-drop node with one circulator and feeding the add channel into its port 3. Light into port 3 goes to port 1, back towards the source; the add path needs the second circulator after the grating. */
